=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed existing code:
- drive_handler.go: Get() returns drive + telemetry + positions inline as map.
  Already uses time.Now() as endTs when drive.EndTs == nil for telemetry/position queries.
  Does NOT compute live summary fields (distance, duration, battery, speed).
- charging_handler.go: Get() returns *models.ChargingSession directly via writeJSON.
  Does NOT compute live summary fields for in-progress sessions.
- signal/redis_cache.go: RedisSignalCache with GetAll(vehicleID) returns all signals from Redis HSET.
- database/signal_log_reader.go: SnapshotAt(vehicleID, at) returns latest signal values at a timestamp.
- converters.go: toFloatOk(), signalFloat(), signalInt() — signal extraction helpers.
- router.go: Already wires Redis cache to maintenance/command/watch handlers via WithRedisCache pattern.
- Frontend: useDrive() / useChargingSessionDetail() have no refetchInterval for live sessions.
  Types: Drive, DriveDetail, ChargingSession — no `live` field.

=== REASONING ===
1. DriveHandler.Get: When EndTs is nil (in-progress), compute live values from:
   - SnapshotAt(drive.StartTs) for start-of-drive state
   - Redis GetAll (sub-ms) for current state, with signal_log fallback
   - Compute: duration (wall clock), distance (odometer delta), battery, speed, position, power, temp
   - Add "live": true to response JSON

2. ChargingHandler.Get: Same pattern:
   - SnapshotAt(session.StartTs) for start battery/energy
   - Redis/signal_log for current battery/energy
   - Compute: duration, battery levels, energy added (ACChargingEnergyIn delta), power
   - Wrap response in map to add "live" field

3. Router: Wire RedisSignalCache to driveHandler and chargingHandler

4. Frontend: Add `live?: boolean` to Drive and ChargingSession types.
   Add refetchInterval callback to useDrive() and useChargingSessionDetail() —
   auto-refetch at INTERVALS.FAST (10s) when live === true.

5. Telemetry/positions for in-progress drives already work (Prompts 24) —
   SignalTracePivotFlat uses time.Now() when end_ts is null.

=== CHANGES ===
Files modified:
1. internal/api/drive_handler.go
   - Added `redisCache *signal.RedisSignalCache` field
   - Added `WithRedisCache` method
   - Modified `Get()`: computes live values via enrichLiveDrive() when EndTs == nil
   - Added `enrichLiveDrive()`: reads start snapshot + current signals, computes
     duration, distance, battery, speed, position, power, temp
   - Added `currentSignals()`: Redis-first with signal_log fallback
   - Added `"live": true/false` to response JSON

2. internal/api/charging_handler.go
   - Added `redisCache *signal.RedisSignalCache` field
   - Added `WithRedisCache` method
   - Modified `Get()`: computes live values via enrichLiveCharge() when IsActive()
   - Added `chargingSessionResponse()`: wraps session in map with `live` field
   - Added `enrichLiveCharge()`: computes duration, battery, energy, power from snapshots
   - Added `currentSignals()`: Redis-first with signal_log fallback

3. internal/api/router.go
   - Wired driveHandler.WithRedisCache(redisSignalCache) and
     chargingHandler.WithRedisCache(redisSignalCache) in Redis wiring block

4. web/src/types/driving.ts
   - Added `live?: boolean` to Drive interface

5. web/src/api/types.ts
   - Added `live?: boolean` to ChargingSession interface

6. web/src/api/hooks/useDriving.ts
   - Added refetchInterval callback to useDrive(): auto-refetches at INTERVALS.FAST when live
   - Imported INTERVALS from constants

7. web/src/api/hooks/useCharging.ts
   - Added refetchInterval callback to useChargingSessionDetail(): auto-refetches when live
   - Imported INTERVALS from constants

